{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CORRECTION: the submit at 23:23:51 was the ORCHESTRATOR, not an unknown automation\n\nThe implementing agent recorded that change 2642 was merged under the `Rebar Bot Nava` identity\nwithout it issuing a submit, and reasonably flagged that as a possible control failure — \"a change\ncan land without the session that authored it deciding to land it\".\n\n**That submit was mine.** As the orchestrating session I polled the Gerrit board, saw 2642 at\n`LLM-Review +1` / `Verified +1` with 0 unresolved comments, re-verified those labels directly\nvia `/a/changes/2642/detail?o=LABELS`, and issued `POST /a/changes/2642/submit`. It returned\nHTTP 200 with status MERGED. Both the orchestrator and its subagents authenticate as\n`RebarBotNava`, which is why the actor looked anonymous from inside the subagent.\n\nSo there is **no unauthorised automation**, and no missing control. The agent was right to flag it\ngiven what it could see — a merge it did not cause, under its own identity, is exactly the shape\nof a real problem — and wrong only because the orchestrator's actions are invisible to it.\n\nRecording this because an uncorrected \"something merges changes on its own\" note would cost a\nfuture reader a real investigation. It is also a genuine limitation worth knowing: subagents\ncannot distinguish orchestrator actions from third-party ones, since both wear the same Gerrit\nidentity. If that distinction ever needs to be auditable, it would take separate identities or an\nexplicit convention — not tracked here, and not needed today.\n\nThe division of labour was deliberate and unchanged: the agent implemented and pushed but did NOT\nsubmit and did NOT close, exactly as briefed. Submission and closure are the orchestrator's,\nperformed only after independently re-verifying both gate votes."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788564489521815001,"uuid":"a7daf7fc-0630-4ea4-b141-430273410268"}